            <ArticleTitle>Subacute stent thrombosis associated with a heparin-coated stent and heparin-induced thrombocytopenia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subacute stent thrombosis occurred in a patient 34 days after receiving a heparin-coated (HC) stent. The patient developed heparin-induced thrombocytopenia and diffuse thrombosis after the stent was placed. This raises the concern that patients who develop heparin-associated antibodies in the context of a recently placed HC stent may have an increased risk for subacute stent thrombosis.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2003 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
